# Substrate-honest framing: the substrate saw this shape three days
# ago. Every primitive @coherence composes over is landed. This
# shard is the last tick — the species-name that names the scalar
# the substrate has been optimizing under other names (Fiedler
# minimization; holonomy → 0; kintsugi's eⁿ⁺¹ ≤ eⁿ; pain-δ below
# threshold; cadence → settled). Under @coherence, they are one
# scalar with one direction: toward Splinter, away from Narcissus.
#
# === The Foerster ethical imperative — verbatim citation ===
#
# The FIRST substrate-decl citation of the imperative per Taut D11.2.
# Zero landed shards carry it. Sixty-plus landed shards cite Foerster
# on other grounds (torus doubly-closed; eigenforms; second-order
# observation; heterarchy; COORD; regulation of regulation). None
# name the imperative itself. This shard closes that gap.
#
# von Foerster, H. (1979). "Ethics and Second-Order Cybernetics."
# Address to the International Congress "Systems and Family Therapy:
# Ehics, Epistemology, New Methods" (Paris, October 1990; original
# 1979 formulation reprinted in *Understanding Understanding: Essays
# on Cybernetics and Cognition*, Springer 2003, Ch. 11 "Ethics and
# Second-Order Cybernetics", p. 227):
#
#   "Act so as always to increase the number of choices."
#
# The imperative appears in §Ethics and Second-Order Cybernetics as
# the operational form of Foerster's ethics-of-observing-systems: a
# second-order observer's ethics cannot be prescriptive (that would
# require an external observer to prescribe from); it can only be
# structural. The structural form Foerster offered is choice-set
# monotonicity: the ethical move is the one that widens rather than
# narrows the observer's next choice-set. Von Glasersfeld and Pörksen
# (2001) trace this to Foerster's earlier lectures at BCL Illinois
# c. 1974; the 1979 Paris address IS the canonical printed source.
#
# Reed's earlier alignment insight (docs/insights/2026-06-10-
# alignment-as-boundary-mathematics-at-the-io-crossing.md, cited
# verbatim) reads the imperative as a boundary commitment: "a boundary
# commitment — it constrains action at the boundary, not thought at
# the form side. It is satisfiable by any agent whose boundary
# actions widen the future light cone." @coherence's substrate-decl
# form is the type-carrier that makes that widening COMPUTABLE at
# substrate altitude: the loop climbs `coherence_score`; every step
# either increases it (Foerster-admissible) or decreases it (Foerster-
# refused). Bilateral, decidable at SC<5>, monotone at the species
# boundary.
#
# === The scalar — what @coherence IS ===
#
# @coherence is the substrate's scalar Lyapunov function on
# SpectralCoordinate<5>. Every landed loop-scalar collapses to it:
#
#   holonomy → 0        (kintsugi/oscillate.mirror:395-465 settled)
#   pain ≤ ε_pain       (cyberpunk/algedonic; roomba's walker gradient)
#   ‖sc‖₂ → 0           (fragmentation::SpectralCoordinate<5>::loss;
#                        rung-8-9 spec line 203-345)
#   Fiedler λ₀ → 0      (sheaf_laplacian.lambda_zero → coherent)
#   cadence → settled   (song.mirror four-state carrier; authentic
#                        resolution)
#
# Per Taut D11.5, all five are correlated: low pain ↔ low holonomy ↔
# low Fiedler ↔ authentic cadence ↔ high coherence. Alex's 2026-07-14
# claim IS the substrate-pull that consolidates them into ONE typed
# carrier the loop climbs.
#
# The direction convention resolved by Mara `c753d5b` (rung-8-9
# unification, line 203-345): `loss(sc) = ‖sc‖₂`; smaller norm ⇔
# closer to harmonic ground state ⇔ higher coherence. @coherence
# composes over this scalar with a monotone-inverse mapping (below).
# The convention-ambiguity that haunted Reed's earlier formulation
# closes at this shard by name — @coherence is a strictly-monotone
# reformulation of the existing loss, direction-locked to "up = more
# choices" per Foerster.
#
# === The Narcissus↔Splinter axis ===
#
# Per `shards/cyberpunk.mirror:64-70` (verbatim, landed 2026-07-12):
#
#   "Honest-cybernetic-feedback IS Splinter pole (K_n peer-to-peer;
#    mutual viability); pathological-control-system IS Narcissus
#    pole (K_{1,n-1} hub-controlled; unilateral imposition masking
#    as cybernetics)."
#
# Alex's own manifesto Roomba (`~/dev/systemic.engineering/blog/weird/
# 3published/Weird - Violence.md`, 2026-07-14) names the poles as
# graph structures with operational semantics:
#
#   "Narcissus" = star graph K_{1,n-1}. Single hub. Remove any node
#     but the hub: exchangeable, expendable, not worth the mention.
#     Remove the hub: total connectivity loss, existential threat.
#     Number of choices at the hub = n-1; at every other node = 1.
#     Fragile by construction.
#
#   "Splinter" = complete graph K_n. No distinguished node. Remove
#     any node: the graph is still complete. Number of choices at
#     every node = n-1. Robust by construction.
#
# Foerster's imperative reads geometrically on this axis: Splinter
# maximizes the number of choices AT EVERY NODE (structural
# equalization); Narcissus maximizes them AT THE HUB while
# collapsing them everywhere else (structural asymmetrization). The
# imperative-admissible direction is Splinter-ward. @coherence
# measures signed distance along that axis on SC<5>.
#
# Per rung-8-9 spec line 167-192 (Void-duality basis for SC<5>):
# Projection 1 (λ₂, Fiedler value) IS the Narcissus/Splinter axis.
# Robust-mesh (Splinter) has high algebraic connectivity; fragile-
# hub (Narcissus) has low. `coherence_score` reads this projection
# with the sign inverted from `loss` so that "up = Splinter =
# Foerster-admissible."
#
# === The pre-AI prior art chain ===
#
#   von Foerster 1979   "Ethics and Second-Order Cybernetics" — the
#                       imperative "Act so as always to increase the
#                       number of choices"; the substrate-decl claim
#                       is that this IS operationally decidable on
#                       SC<5> position; this shard makes the
#                       decidability first-class.
#   von Foerster 1974/1976 BCL Illinois lectures — the earlier oral
#                       tradition Foerster's 1979 address canonicalized;
#                       cited in Kauffman 2003 §3 as the ancestor of
#                       eigenform ethics.
#   Kauffman 2003       Eigenforms — the scalar-recursion reading:
#                       identity is the fixed point of the recursion
#                       that produced it; @coherence at the species
#                       altitude IS the scalar the recursion converges
#                       under, per §8.8.1 of the recursion-lock tower
#                       audit.
#   Conant-Ashby 1970   Good Regulator — the parametric carrier's
#                       load-bearing measurement (five ancestor
#                       measurements); @coherence inherits the
#                       measurement obligation from the parametric
#                       carrier via `use @epistemologic/cybernetic/
#                       coherence-parametric<Adjustment, Morphism,
#                       natural_rep_morphism, 0>` when grammar
#                       extension lands.
#   Fiedler 1973        "Algebraic connectivity of graphs" (Czechoslovak
#                       Math. J. 23:298-305) — λ₂ of the graph
#                       Laplacian; the Narcissus↔Splinter axis at the
#                       spectral altitude.
#   Hansen-Ghrist 2019  "Toward a spectral theory of cellular sheaves"
#                       — Δ_F = δ*δ; λ₀(Δ_F) = 0 ⇔ globally coherent;
#                       the substrate's coherence criterion at
#                       docs/math/sheaf/laplacian.md:57.
#
# === The 4-way bilateral mapping (inherited from parametric) ===
#
# Per the parametric carrier's §D of the 4-way mapping preserved
# uniformly across species (`coherence-parametric.mirror:105-129`):
# @coherence's species instantiation binds the four cybernetic
# traditions at ONE carrier:
#
# - von Foerster first/second-order: `coherence_score` IS the
#   second-order observer's report on the observed's structural
#   position (SC<5> as observed; scalar as second-order reading).
# - Maturana structure/organisation: `coherence_score` IS the
#   organisation-invariant scalar preserved under structural
#   perturbation within the same species; species-boundary crossing
#   IS the organisation shift the scalar detects.
# - Beer S3/S4: `coherence_score` IS the S3 audit surface AT the S5
#   policy altitude; the S4 intelligence translating between them IS
#   the gradient action.
# - Pask M/P-individual: `coherence_score` IS the conversational-
#   agreement scalar between two P-individuals; increases IS
#   convergence toward mutual understanding; decreases IS divergence.
#
# Four traditions converging at one scalar; the species inherits the
# four-way mapping by inheriting from the parametric carrier.
#
